==English==
{{wp|[[+#People|+]]}}

===Etymology===
* As an English and Scottish surname, from the noun {{m|en|doe}}.
* As a {{der|en|nrf|-}} surname, from {{der|en|fro|d'}} {{m|fro|Eu}}, from {{w|Eu, Seine-Maritime}}. That city's name could be from {{der|en|frk|*auwju|t=island, water meadow}} or otherwise a reduction of {{der|en|la|Augusta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dəʊ/|a=UK}}
* {{enPR|dō|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/doʊ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊ|s=1}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop|s}}

# {{surname|en}} of [[English]] origin.
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Elizabeth Wagmeister|title=Jay-Z says inconsistencies in rape accuser’s story proves her attorney was looking for ‘money and fame’|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/12/14/entertainment/jay-z-lawsuit-response|date=2024-12-14|passage=In the amended complaint, Carter is accused of raping the then-13-year-old Jane '''Doe''' at an afterparty for the MTV Video Music Awards in the year 2000.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260106204323/https://www.cnn.com/2024/12/14/entertainment/jay-z-lawsuit-response|archivedate=6 January 2026}}

====Usage notes====
This is often used as a [[pseudonymous]] surname.

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|English-language pseudonymous surname}} {{l|en|Roe}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|John Doe}}
* {{l|en|Jane Doe}}
* {{l|en|Juan Doe}}
* {{l|en|Juanita Doe}}

====Statistics====
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''Doe'' is the 4972<sup>nd</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 179 individuals. ''Doe'' is most common among White (54.91%) and Black/African-American (29.9%) individuals.

